<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - NatWest sees higher Danish '97 GDP growth.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - NatWest sees higher Danish '97 GDP growth.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey Britain's Nat West Markets on Monday raised its expectations for Denmark's 1997 GDP (gross domestic product) growth to 3.2 percent from 3.0 percent in its last forecast in April.</p>
<p>At the same time it lowered its inflation forecast for this year to 2.4 percent from 2.6 percent, raising to 9.5 billion crowns its previous estimate of a current account surplus of 8.3 billion crowns</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in May foresaw 3.3 percent GDP growth, 2.3 percent inflation, 7.8 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 12.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations in recent months.</p>
<p>	  (pct)	 GDP    inflation  unemployment c/a (bln Dkk)</p>
<p>NatWest (5/97)	3.2    2.4	  7.9	    9.5</p>
<p>Sydbank (5/97)	3.0    2.2	  7.9	   14.9</p>
<p>BG Bank (5/97)	3.3    2.4	  7.7	    7.0</p>
<p>IBJ (5/97)	    3.0    2.0	  7.9	   12.2</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley (5/97) 3.5  2.4	  8.0	     --</p>
<p>M.Grenfell (5/97)   3.1    2.3	  7.9	   12.0</p>
<p>Salomon (5/97)	2.7    2.4	  --	     8.0</p>
<p>Nykredit (5/97)     2.6    2.1	  8.2	   10.0</p>
<p>Spar Nord (5/97)    2.9    2.4	  7.8	   13.0</p>
<p>Danish Ind Conf (5/97) 2.7 2.1	  --	    12.1</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
